# PR draft vs ready for review

**Default:** create pull requests as **Draft** (early visibility, branch CI, WIP commits). **Draft = do not review** — implementation or verification may still be in flight.

**Agent handoff (typical):** When the feature is implemented, tested, deployed on cloud/sandbox, and the **embedded `.mp4`** + **What to look for** bullets are synced via [obsidian-pr-ship-sync](../../skills/obsidian-pr-ship-sync/SKILL.md), **stop in Draft** and tell Adrian the PR is ready for **human** review. Do **not** auto-mark Ready unless the user explicitly asked.

Mark **Ready for review** only when you would ask a teammate to review **now** (usually **Adrian** after watching the demo): stated scope is done, self-reviewed diff, title/description complete, CI green (or failures explained), and demo embeds match shipped code.

**Before Ready (when marking Ready is requested):** run **[obsidian-pr-ship-sync](../../skills/obsidian-pr-ship-sync/SKILL.md)** in the same turn so title, description, and embedded media match **shipped code and the latest recording**:

1. **`ManagePullRequest` `update_pr`** — full body + artifacts + **What to look for** bullets.
2. **`ManagePullRequest` `update_pr`** — **`draft: false`** only after step 1 and explicit go-ahead to mark Ready.

Do not mark Ready with stale copy or embeds from an older run. After substantive post-review changes or merge-conflict fixes, **convert back to Draft**, then **Ready** again ([GitHub stage docs](https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/proposing-changes-to-your-work-with-pull-requests/changing-the-stage-of-a-pull-request)).

## Checklist before Ready

| Gate | Ready when |
|------|------------|
| Scope | Goal implemented; no hidden pre-merge TODO unless called out in the description |
| Diff | Full self-review; body explains **what** and **why** |
| Tests / CI | Repo `typecheck` / `test` / `build` green on the PR branch |
| Deploy | Sandbox/cloud Obsidian verify done when the change runs in-app (not local-only when cloud is available) |
| UI / behavior | When [pr-product-demos](./pr-product-demos.mdc) applies: embedded cloud **`.mp4`**, [obsidian-ui-visibility](../../skills/obsidian-ui-visibility/SKILL.md) + jank pass during record ([obsidian-visual-verify](../../skills/obsidian-visual-verify/SKILL.md), [ux-design](../../skills/ux-design/SKILL.md)) |
| PR ship sync | Body and embeds match **this** branch and **this** demo ([obsidian-pr-ship-sync](../../skills/obsidian-pr-ship-sync/SKILL.md)) |
| Size | Large PRs: description tells reviewers where to start; split if unfair to review |

**Lighten** for docs-only, zero-behavior dependency bumps, or explicit **`/no-test`** — still state what was verified in the PR body.

## Human verify (maintainer)

Adrian marks **Ready** when satisfied with the demo and diff. Agents should not ask for merge until the PR is **Ready** (when the user uses that workflow) and merge conflicts/CI are clean.

**Note:** GitHub **draft release** (release workflow) is unrelated to **draft pull request** — see [obsidian-plugin-dev](../../skills/obsidian-plugin-dev/SKILL.md) release notes.

